  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1107 AM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will become established over the Southern\nPlains this week, while a large surface high extends from Eastern\nCanada into much of the Plains. Dry weather with a slow warming\ntrend can be expected as daytime highs trend back above normal. \n\nA low amplitude wave is expected to top the ridge this weekend,\nand bring the next chance for showers and thunderstorms. A\npotentially more significant system continues to show up in the \nmedium range model data next week, likely arriving beyond this \nforecast.",
